      trivia: "Belinda was loved between the wars by the king of comedy Groucho Marx; according to his son Arthur, his father always kept to hand a box of outsize 'Belindas' — a sight later likened to 'small Scud missiles'. Founded by Francisco Menéndez in 1882, this distinguished house merged with Punch in 1897 and passed to Fernández y Palicio in 1930. The Honduran version belongs to the Villazon / Estelo Padrón lineage that produced Hoyo de Monterrey."
